{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland","id":36314,"title":"Oz, Neverland and Wonderland","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-24T05:47:20-08:00","id":36314,"title":"Oz, Neverland and Wonderland","content":"These have become pretty much the three iconic modern 'fairylands' , and thus fair game for Changeling. Has anyone got any ideas about how to use Peter Pan, The Wizard of Oz or Alice and Wonderland in Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T06:36:50-08:00","id":36341,"title":"","content":"For peter pan, you absolutely cannot do better than reading the original stories and playing Pan as a True Fae. You don't need to make him darker, in fact it's better if you don't. In fact, if you watch Once Upon a Time's version of Pan, he's actually less (I won't quite say evil because that implies maturity) than the original!<br /> <br /> Wonderland is a very hard one since the entire point is that there's no plot, reason nor logic to anything that happens there. I would probably use it as a guideline for running dreams, in that nothing makes sense (not even symbolically, sorry Mages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but if you go with the flow and play along with the nonsense you can usually get what you wanted. (By that logic, Alice is a pretty incompetent dream traveller.) You can also base hobgoblins, true fae or low Clarity Changeling's behaviour on the characters.<br /> <br /> One thing, don't try to run your own adoption of Alice. I have never seen a single one that comes even close to the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T18:44:11-08:00","id":36666,"title":"","content":"If you watch once upon a time, their depiction of peter pan is perfect for a keeper IMO. So I recommend watching that show, season 3 the current one, for ideas. Their depication of Wonderland in the spin-off show IMO would be good for ideas for the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T14:30:03-08:00","id":40155,"title":"","content":"Also, take a look at <a href=\"http://namesakecomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Namesake</a> for inspiration: the first story arc was essentially \u201cEmma goes to Oz\u201d, and the current cast of characters includes Alice. It\u2019s not technically Changeling; but it\u2019s remarkably close. <br /> <br /> For a dark and twisted take on Oz, I\u2019d also recommend the Wicked Years series: Wicked, Son of a Witch, A Lion Among Men, and Out of Oz. The Wicked Years is interesting in that it shows a faerieland after its Keeper has been deposed. The results ain\u2019t pretty. <br /> <br /> For Peter Pan, I\u2019d be inclined to say that he was originally a changeling, but that by the time he met Wendy he had become a True Fae and established Wonderland. (And yes, his Once Upon A Time counterpart was weak compared to the real thing. That show had a good first season; but it lost its way in the second season, and never regained its footing.)<br /> <br /> Henson\u2019s Labyrinth is another good faerieland to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T07:11:07-08:00","id":40493,"title":"","content":"On page 28 of &quot;Power Within the Land&quot; R. J. Stewart describes a technique consisting of three basic stages:<br /> <br /> 1. Sit in silence for a few moments, stilling your sense of time, space and interactions or events.<br /> <br /> 2. Following the imagery of the narrative, which should be heard, with your eyes closed. You enter into the story and travel through it, returning to your starting point.<br /> <br /> 3. On conclusion, sit in silence for a few moments and reorientate yourself and, if preferred, make notes.<br /> <br /> The narrative he's talking about are folk and fairy tales, but I don't see why a chapter from &quot;The Wizard of Oz&quot;, &quot;Peter Pan&quot;, or &quot;Alice in Wonderland&quot; wouldn't do just as well.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If your troupe has three members they can take turns reading a chapter from each book to their fellow troupe members and the storyteller. If your troupe has four to six members you can add in one to three collections of folk or fairy tales to the mix. If the storyteller or any of the troupe members are artistically inclined they can draw whatever impressions spirng to mind creating a map of your local otherworld. Of course this technique would work for any roleplaying game not just Changeling.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T19:15:05-07:00","id":96657,"title":"","content":"Of course you can always look at how others have re-invisioned the stories and take ideas from them. The book and the play Wicked for example. The show &quot;Once Upon a Time&quot; mentioned above and it's spin-off &quot;Wonderland&quot;. There are also the comic books: The Oz/Wonderland Chronicles from <a href=\"http://buymetoys.com\" target=\"_blank\">Buy Me Toys</a>; Legend of Oz: the Wicked West from <a href=\"http://bigdogink.com\" target=\"_blank\">Big Dog Ink</a>; and Tales from Oz by <a href=\"http://zenescope.com\" target=\"_blank\">Zenescope</a>. Zenescope also has Wonderland and Neverland titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T20:10:21-07:00","id":96686,"title":"","content":"Bare with me on this. What if Captain Hook is a Changeling, the catch is he is the one boy that Escaped Peter Pan, and that is why he seeks to kill Peter Pan, because he doesn't want the Fate of the Lost Boys to befall any other.<br /> <br /> Hmm what would be good for him? A Draconic? A Wizened Soldier? Perhaps Draconic would fit, and if he never escaped maybe he would have been a Beast instead like the other lost boys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T01:39:59-07:00","id":96773,"title":"","content":"Fairest duelist, Fairest swashbuckler, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T17:09:33-07:00","id":97884,"title":"","content":"I'd peg Hook as a particularly genteel Cyclopean, what's with the obvious physical handicap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T17:15:48-07:00","id":97887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland?p=96773#post96773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairest duelist, Fairest swashbuckler, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were those Kiths? I forgot many of them, so I just figured Draconic would be the closest Fairest Kith I could think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:12:08-07:00","id":99496,"title":"","content":"For Captain Hook, I'd go with a Darkling Razorhand. He's pretty and all, but I see him as far more ruthless. In my storyline I did what Eldagusto mentioned--Captain Hook was a Lost Boy (in our story there was romance between them) who was left behind on an adventure. Because he was in a different territory, he aged. He grew bitter and resentful, and has sought revenge ever since. Peter himself we ran as having always been True Fae. He would periodically become enamored with the mortal world and become a changeling, but eventually he'd grow bored and return to Arcadia. Hook is pretty BA, to be able to survive in Arcadia for so long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T15:35:55-07:00","id":99545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland?p=97887#post97887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were those Kiths? I forgot many of them, so I just figured Draconic would be the closest Fairest Kith I could think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Dark Eara (probably)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T15:50:53-07:00","id":99554,"title":"","content":"Those do not exist as Kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T16:06:10-07:00","id":99563,"title":"","content":"Patience Arc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Musketeer Changeling is coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>