/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T01:08:39-07:00","id":99823,"title":"","content":"How can you have a setting based on the musketeers without a swashbuckling kith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:55:17-07:00","id":103534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland?p=99584#post99584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we get another fucking Fairest Kith, I'm going to go nuts.<br /> <br /> Seriously, like four out of five from Grim Fears were Fairest, and I'm still mad about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not alone!<br /> <br /> So, in your opinion, which was worse: Romancer or Playmate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:25:01-07:00","id":103727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland?p=103534#post103534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not alone!<br /> <br /> So, in your opinion, which was worse: Romancer or Playmate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Playmate's not bad(I actually don't have much issue with the kiths themselves), but it is probably the worst one of the bunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T01:06:14-07:00","id":107321,"title":"","content":"My brother is playing a Lost Boy who's Keeper was Peter Pan in our local Accord game. Otherwise, for Gentry in Wonderland, a good choice, thanks to Disney, is the Queen of Hearts, expecting everything to go her way in the realm. Also, the new book, Dorothy Must Die, is also interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T13:05:17-07:00","id":107629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thornfield13713</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland#post36314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These have become pretty much the three iconic modern 'fairylands' , and thus fair game for Changeling. Has anyone got any ideas about how to use Peter Pan, The Wizard of Oz or Alice and Wonderland in Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div> I've had a game where Summer was Neverland, Autumn was Oz, Wonderland was Spring, and Enchanted Forest (typical fairy tale characters) was Winter. I mean, come on. Snow White is perfect name for a Winter Queen.<br /> <br /> It makes a nice little circle, there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Snow White, the Fairest Winter Queen <br /> Alice, the Beast Spring Queen<br /> Captain Hook, the Ogre Summer King<br /> Dorothy, the Wizened Autumn Queen<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T11:27:26-07:00","id":109479,"title":"","content":"Being a CtL storyteller with oz tattoos my players kinda expect at the very least an easter egg to something oz themed in my changeling chronicles. Taking Oz as a whole and using it as a setting in Arcadia seems to work out fairly seamlessly (maps of oz are very easy to come by). But what I've found to be most interesting is using off beat oz characters (and there's PLENTY to choose from) and tossing them in here and there. Most recently I've designed a &quot;hit squad&quot; motley to handle privateers around the tin-man, scarecrow, and lion. However dropping the three with no modifications tends to lean towards boring or predictable. Years back mcfarlene toys produced an oz toy line that I've used more then once as inspiration for incorporating Oz into a CtL game (<a href=\"http://www.spawn.com/toys/series.aspx?series=184\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.spawn.com/toys/series.aspx?series=184</a>) and <a href=\"http://righttodream.digitaldreaming.org/ozframe.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://righttodream.digitaldreaming.org/ozframe.html</a> has more then a plethora of interesting Oz setting material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2681-lousilvers","name":"LouSilvers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T11:34:42-07:00","id":109485,"title":"","content":"I remember both of those links! Good onya!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T12:22:28-07:00","id":112166,"title":"","content":"just make sure to give them a real world modern twist, <br /> <br /> Peter Pan could be a rouge changeling anarchist who recruits children to sabatoge and commit terrorist attacks on the gentry or even a local free hold<br /> The Queen of hearts is a soulless who keeps a littleral jar of hearts in her luggage (and not in a once upon a time magical curse kind of way)<br /> Mabey Dorthy, the lion, the tin man and the scarecrow are now the changeling version seal team six? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T12:23:53-07:00","id":112168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/36314-oz-neverland-and-wonderland?p=112166#post112166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just make sure to give them a real world modern twist,<br /> <br /> Peter Pan could be a rouge changeling anarchist who recruits children to sabatoge and commit terrorist attacks on the gentry or even a local free hold<br /> The Queen of hearts is a soulless who keeps a littleral jar of hearts in her luggage (and not in a once upon a time magical curse kind of way)<br /> Mabey Dorthy, the lion, the tin man and the scarecrow are now the changeling version seal team six?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ha, well done, yeah they were Oz's premier assassins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}